Let me update the `getHomeFeeds()` implementation in the RemoteRepositoryImpl class:

```kotlin:app/src/main/java/tungp/android/bazarbooks/data/repository/RemoteRepositoryImpl.kt
override suspend fun getHomeFeeds(): Flow<BazaResult<HomeFeedsDomainModel>> = flow {
 emit(BazaResult.Loading)
 try {
 val response = apiService.getHomeFeeds()
 if (response.statusCode == 200 && response.data != null) {
 // Convert API response to domain model
 val domainModel = response.data.toDomainModel()
 emit(BazaResult.Success(domainModel))
 } else {
 emit(BazaResult.Error(response.message ?: "Unknown error occurred"))
 }
 } catch (e: Exception) {
 emit(BazaResult.Error(e.message ?: "Network error occurred"))
 }
}
```

I've made these key changes:
1. Added the `suspend` modifier to match the interface definition
2. Completed the implementation with proper error handling
3. Added conversion from API response to domain model (assuming a `toDomainModel()` extension function exists)
4. Properly emitting success and error states through the Flow

Note that you may need to create a mapper/extension function that converts your API response model to the `HomeFeedsDomainModel` if it doesn't already exist."}]}

